I've left out the `http-client` import and the enrichment fetch. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, and the graph definition has not been updated to add HTTP. The fetch would also send each item's untrusted feed text to an external host. The implementation below covers the granted behavior: it drops items whose ids are already in the `seen` store.

```wit
package gen:node;

use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| crate::aap::caps::state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

